## Why This Is Asked
Tests the candidate's ability to define a data-driven CAPA program for supply-chain vulnerabilities in multi-region systems, balancing traceability, regional scoping, and automated rollout.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data modeling with SBOM, CVEs, tenants, regions
- Region-aware lifecycle state machines
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces
- Metrics for containment, recurrence, MTTR
- RCA templates and canary rollout controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal TypeScript types for CAPA
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenants: string[];
  region: string;
  cveId: string;
  sbom: string;
  logs: string[];
  containment: string;
  correctiveAction: string;
  preventiveAction: string;
  rca: string;
  status: 'detected'|'triaged'|'contained'|'eradicated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model time-to-containment vs time-to-eradication in your metrics?
- What governance ensures SBOM accuracy across auto-updates?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of drift in a multi-tenant streaming system with region isolation, ensuring containment without collateral impact. It also probes data lineage, governance, and rollout discipline.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with tenant scope, region, evidence, ownership, and lineage
- Region-tenant gated lifecycle to prevent cross-tenant bleed
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with linked logs/traces
- Tenant-scoped metrics: containment MTTR, drift score, recurrence rate, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollback plan for sessionization logic changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: CAPA data model (conceptual)
class CAPA {
  constructor(id, tenantId, region) {
    this.id = id;
    this.tenantId = tenantId;
    this.region = region;
    this.evidence = [];
    this.rootCause = null;
    this.actions = [];
    this.owner = null;
    this.state = 'DETECTED';
    this.timestamps = {};
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test isolation between tenants during a canary rollout?
- How would you handle cross-tenant drift if tenants share resources?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests CAPA fundamentals under real-world data issues: region awareness, basic data modeling, and a simple remediation flow.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model, lifecycle, REST API, regional metrics, RCA, canary.
- Trade-offs: latency of detection vs noise, data retention for evidence.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express REST endpoints
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let store = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res)=>{ const cap={id:Date.now().toString(), ...req.body, status:'detected', created_at:new Date().toISOString()}; store.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
app.put('/caps/:id', (req,res)=>{ const idx=store.findIndex(c=>c.id===req.params.id); if(idx>=0){store[idx]={...store[idx], ...req.body}; res.json(store[idx]);} else res.status(404).end();});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and test the canary plan before broader rollout?
- What telemetry would you capture to ensure no regression after remediation?

